        "original_id": "5af80e1b-9481-59d5-b8d0-2a5a447d05cf",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John du Pont, Dave Schultz, Mark Schultz, Corey Jantzen\n- Works: Foxcatcher\n- Topics: freestyle wrestling, Team Foxcatcher\n\nFacts:\n- Dave Schultz was born on June 6, 1959.\n- In 1986, John du Pont recruited 1984 U.S. Olympic gold medalist brothers Mark Schultz and Dave Schultz to help coach U.S. wrestlers for national, world, and Olympic competition.\n- The film Foxcatcher is loosely based on John du Pont’s 1986 recruitment of Mark Schultz and Dave Schultz and the later murder of Dave Schultz.\n- Dave Schultz was an American Olympic and world champion freestyle wrestler and a seven-time World and Olympic medalist.\n- John du Pont murdered Dave Schultz in January 1996.\n- Dave Schultz died on January 26, 1996.\n- Corey Jantzen worked on the Academy Award-nominated film Foxcatcher, where he played a wrestler on Team Foxcatcher and helped choreograph the wrestling sequences.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
